# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Design principles of operator representations {#design-principles-of-operator-representations}"
msgstr "Mga prinsipyo sa disenyo ng mga operator representation {#design-principles-of-operator-representations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains the common design principles and core concepts shared across all operator representations in the [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapaliwanag ng gabay na ito ang mga karaniwang prinsipyo sa disenyo at pangunahing konsepto na ibinabahagi ng lahat ng operator representation sa [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators#module-qiskit_fermions.operators \"qiskit_fermions.operators\") module.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Pangkalahatang-ideya {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operator representations provided by this module share several fundamental design principles:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga operator representation na ibinibigay ng module na ito ay may iisang ilang pangunahing prinsipyo sa disenyo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Sparse data structure**](#sparse-term-representation): Operators encode only non-identity operations. The internal data layout is generally inspired by sparse matrix data formats, enabling efficient storage and computation for systems with many modes but relatively few significant contributions.\n"
msgstr "[**Sparse data structure**](#sparse-term-representation): Ang mga operator ay nag-e-encode lang ng mga operasyong hindi identity. Ang panloob na layout ng data ay karaniwang hango sa mga sparse matrix data format, na nagbibigay-daan sa episyenteng storage at computation para sa mga sistemang maraming mode pero kaunti lang ang makabuluhang kontribusyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Term iteration and reconstruction**](#term-iteration-and-reconstruction): Irrespective of the internal sparse storage, operators provide a consistent iteration interface, so you can inspect, filter, and transform terms without understanding the underlying data structure, then reconstruct new operators from modified terms.\n"
msgstr "[**Term iteration at reconstruction**](#term-iteration-and-reconstruction): Anuman ang panloob na sparse storage, nagbibigay ang mga operator ng pare-parehong iteration interface, kaya maaari mong siyasatin, i-filter, at i-transform ang mga term nang hindi kailangang unawain ang pinagbabatayang istruktura ng data, at saka bumuo ng mga bagong operator mula sa mga binagong term.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Mode-based indexing**](#mode-based-indexing): Operators use abstract mode indices to label fermionic degrees of freedom, enabling flexible mapping from physical systems to the operator representation.\n"
msgstr "[**Mode-based indexing**](#mode-based-indexing): Gumagamit ang mga operator ng abstract na mode index para i-label ang mga fermionic degree of freedom, na nagbibigay-daan sa flexible na pag-map mula sa mga pisikal na sistema papunta sa operator representation.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Term grouping and commutation relationships**](#term-grouping): Operators natively support grouping information that associates terms with group indices. This enables optimizations and physical structure preservation without requiring separate data structures. See the [grouping guide](grouping#grouping-explanation) for practical usage.\n"
msgstr "[**Term grouping at mga ugnayan ng commutation**](#term-grouping): Native na sinusuportahan ng mga operator ang grouping information na nag-uugnay sa mga term sa mga group index. Nagbibigay-daan ito sa mga optimization at pagpapanatili ng pisikal na istruktura nang hindi nangangailangan ng hiwalay na mga data structure. Tingnan ang [grouping guide](grouping#grouping-explanation) para sa praktikal na paggamit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Arithmetic and mathematical operations**](#arithmetic-and-mathematical-operations): All operators implement a consistent set of arithmetic operations (such as addition, multiplication, and composition) and mathematical functions by using the [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, enabling uniform code across different operator types.\n"
msgstr "[**Arithmetic at mga mathematical na operasyon**](#arithmetic-and-mathematical-operations): Nagpapatupad ang lahat ng operator ng pare-parehong set ng mga arithmetic na operasyon (tulad ng addition, multiplication, at composition) at mga mathematical function gamit ang [`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, na nagbibigay-daan sa pare-parehong code sa iba't ibang uri ng operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Operator term ordering and normal forms**](#operator-term-ordering): Mathematically equivalent operators can have very different representations and behavior in quantum algorithms. All operator representations support various normal forms (based on algebra-specific commutation relations) to achieve canonical, predictable, and optimizable operator representations.\n"
msgstr "[**Pagkakasunod-sunod ng term ng operator at mga normal form**](#operator-term-ordering): Ang mga operator na katumbas sa matematika ay maaaring may napakaibang representasyon at pag-uugali sa mga quantum algorithm. Sinusuportahan ng lahat ng operator representation ang iba't ibang normal form (batay sa mga commutation relation na partikular sa algebra) para makamit ang canonical, predictable, at ma-optimize na mga operator representation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sparse-term-representation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sparse data structure {#sparse-data-structure}"
msgstr "Istruktura ng sparse data {#sparse-data-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All operators use a **sparse representation** where only non-identity operations are tracked. Each non-identity operation consists of a **coefficient** (complex number) and a **sequence of actions** on specific modes.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang lahat ng operator ng **sparse na representasyon** kung saan sinusubaybayan lang ang mga operasyong hindi identity. Ang bawat operasyong hindi identity ay binubuo ng isang **coefficient** (complex number) at isang **sequence ng mga action** sa mga partikular na mode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This approach dramatically reduces memory usage and computation time, especially for systems with many modes but relatively few significant contributions. By encoding only non-identity operations, operations focus only on what matters, enabling work with large systems that would be infeasible with dense representations. Additionally, operators naturally scale to any number of modes; an operator acting on modes `{0, 1}` works unchanged in systems with many more modes since unaffected modes are implicitly identity.\n"
msgstr "Lubos na binabawasan ng pamamaraang ito ang paggamit ng memory at oras ng computation, lalo na para sa mga sistemang maraming mode pero kaunti lang ang makabuluhang kontribusyon. Dahil nag-e-encode lang ng mga operasyong hindi identity, nakatuon lang ang mga operasyon sa mahalaga, na nagbibigay-daan sa pagtatrabaho sa malalaking sistema na hindi magagawa gamit ang dense na representasyon. Bukod pa rito, natural na nag-i-scale ang mga operator sa anumang bilang ng mode; ang operator na kumikilos sa mga mode na `{0, 1}` ay gumagana nang walang pagbabago sa mga sistemang mas maraming mode dahil ang mga hindi apektadong mode ay implicit na identity.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Identical terms are preserved separately during arithmetic operations and must be explicitly combined if needed.\n"
msgstr "Ang magkakaparehong term ay pinananatiling hiwalay sa mga arithmetic na operasyon at kailangang isama nang tahasan kung kinakailangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Internal storage format {#internal-storage-format}"
msgstr "Panloob na format ng storage {#internal-storage-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Internally, operators are stored in arrays inspired by sparse matrix data formats:\n"
msgstr "Sa loob, iniimbak ang mga operator sa mga array na hango sa mga sparse matrix data format:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Coefficients array**: The complex coefficient for each term\n"
msgstr "**Coefficients array**: Ang complex coefficient ng bawat term\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Mode indices array**: The fermionic modes that each action acts upon\n"
msgstr "**Mode indices array**: Ang mga fermionic mode na kinikilos ng bawat action\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Boundaries array**: Indices marking where each term’s modes begin and end in the mode array\n"
msgstr "**Boundaries array**: Mga index na nagmamarka kung saan nagsisimula at nagtatapos ang mga mode ng bawat term sa mode array\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Additional arrays might be present depending on the operator type. For example, [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") instances include an **actions array** of booleans that specifies the type of fermionic action acting on the respective mode index. In contrast, the `MajoranaOperator` class does not require this distinction since it encodes that information in the parity of the mode index. See the API documentation for your operator type to understand the full storage format.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Maaaring may mga karagdagang array depende sa uri ng operator. Halimbawa, ang mga instance ng [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") ay may kasamang **actions array** ng mga boolean na tumutukoy sa uri ng fermionic action na kumikilos sa kaukulang mode index. Sa kabilang banda, hindi nangangailangan ng pagkakaibang ito ang `MajoranaOperator` class dahil ine-encode nito ang impormasyong iyon sa parity ng mode index. Tingnan ang API documentation ng uri ng iyong operator para maunawaan ang buong storage format.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following examples show how these arrays are organized. First is a direct construction using the sparse arrays:\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng mga sumusunod na halimbawa kung paano inaayos ang mga array na ito. Una ang direktang konstruksyon gamit ang mga sparse array:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs group=\"code\">\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"python\" label=\"PYTHON\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Construct operators directly using sparse arrays\n"
"    >>> # First operator: 1.0 * +0 -1\n"
"    >>> op1 = FermionOperator(\n"
"    ...     coeffs=[1.0],\n"
"    ...     actions=[True, False],\n"
"    ...     modes=[0, 1],\n"
"    ...     boundaries=[0, 2],\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Second operator: 1.0 * +2 -3\n"
"    >>> op2 = FermionOperator(\n"
"    ...     coeffs=[1.0],\n"
"    ...     actions=[True, False],\n"
"    ...     modes=[2, 3],\n"
"    ...     boundaries=[0, 2],\n"
"    ... )\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Combine the sparse operators\n"
"    >>> op1 += op2\n"
"    >>> print(format(op1))\n"
"      1.000000e0 +0.000000e0j * (+0 -1)\n"
"      1.000000e0 +0.000000e0j * (+2 -3)\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  <TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"
msgstr "  <TabItem value=\"c\" label=\"C\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    #include <qiskit_fermions.h>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Construct first operator: 1.0 * +0 -1\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeff1[1] = {{1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions1[2] = {true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes1[2] = {0, 1};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries1[2] = {0, 2};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op1 = qf_ferm_op_new(1, 2, coeff1, actions1, modes1, boundaries1);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Construct first operator: 1.0 * +0 -1\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeff1[1] = {{1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions1[2] = {true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes1[2] = {0, 1};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries1[2] = {0, 2};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op1 = qf_ferm_op_new(1, 2, coeff1, actions1, modes1, boundaries1);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Construct second operator: 1.0 * +2 -3\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeff2[1] = {{1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions2[2] = {true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes2[2] = {2, 3};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries2[2] = {0, 2};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op2 = qf_ferm_op_new(1, 2, coeff2, actions2, modes2, boundaries2);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Construct second operator: 1.0 * +2 -3\n"
"    QkComplex64 coeff2[1] = {{1.0, 0.0}};\n"
"    bool actions2[2] = {true, false};\n"
"    uint32_t modes2[2] = {2, 3};\n"
"    uint32_t boundaries2[2] = {0, 2};\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *op2 = qf_ferm_op_new(1, 2, coeff2, actions2, modes2, boundaries2);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    // Combine the sparse operators. There is no in-place add in the C API, so\n"
"    // the sum is a new operator that the caller owns.\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *sum = qf_ferm_op_add(op1, op2);\n"
msgstr ""
"    // Combine the sparse operators. There is no in-place add in the C API, so\n"
"    // the sum is a new operator that the caller owns.\n"
"    QfFermionOperator *sum = qf_ferm_op_add(op1, op2);\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    qf_ferm_op_free(op1);\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(op2);\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(sum);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    qf_ferm_op_free(op1);\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(op2);\n"
"    qf_ferm_op_free(sum);\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Convenient construction methods {#convenient-construction-methods}"
msgstr "Mga convenient na paraan ng pagbuo {#convenient-construction-methods}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For Python developers, several convenient construction methods are available that abstract away the sparse storage details. These make it easier to build operators without worrying about managing coefficient, mode, and boundary arrays:\n"
msgstr "Para sa mga Python developer, may ilang convenient na paraan ng pagbuo na nagtatago ng mga detalye ng sparse storage. Mas madali nitong mabubuo ang mga operator nang hindi mo na kailangang asikasuhin ang mga array ng coefficient, mode, at boundary:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator, cre, ann\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Construct operators using operator algebra notation\n"
"    >>> op1 = FermionOperator.from_dict({(cre(0), ann(1)): 1.0})\n"
"    >>> op2 = FermionOperator.from_dict({(cre(2), ann(3)): 1.0})\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # The result is sparse even when combining them\n"
"    >>> op1 += op2\n"
"    >>> print(format(op1))\n"
"    1.000000e0 +0.000000e0j * (+0 -1)\n"
"    1.000000e0 +0.000000e0j * (+2 -3)\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // The C API uses direct array construction; convenience methods are not available.\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Individual operator implementations might support additional construction methods suited to their specific use case. Check the API documentation for your operator type to see all available construction options.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Maaaring may karagdagang mga paraan ng pagbuo ang bawat implementasyon ng operator na akma sa partikular nitong gamit. Tingnan ang API documentation ng uri ng operator mo para makita ang lahat ng available na opsyon sa pagbuo.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"id1\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Term iteration and reconstruction {#term-iteration-and-reconstruction}"
msgstr "Pag-iterate ng mga term at muling pagbuo {#term-iteration-and-reconstruction}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operators provide a consistent iteration interface by using [`OperatorTrait.iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\") irrespective of their internal sparse representation. You can therefore inspect, filter, or transform terms without needing to understand the underlying data structure. You can then reconstruct a new operator from the transformed terms by using [`OperatorTrait.from_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.from_terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.from_terms\").\n"
msgstr "Nagbibigay ang mga operator ng pare-parehong interface sa pag-iterate gamit ang [`OperatorTrait.iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\"), kahit ano pa ang internal na sparse representation nila. Kaya puwede mong suriin, i-filter, o baguhin ang mga term nang hindi kailangang intindihin ang pinagbabatayang estruktura ng data. Pagkatapos, puwede kang bumuo ng bagong operator mula sa mga binagong term gamit ang [`OperatorTrait.from_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.from_terms \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.from_terms\").\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```python\n"
"    >>> from qiskit_fermions.operators import FermionOperator, cre, ann\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Construct an operator with terms of different orders\n"
"    >>> op = FermionOperator.from_dict({\n"
"    ...     (): 0.5,  # constant term (order 0)\n"
"    ...     (cre(0), ann(1)): 1.0,  # two-body term (order 2)\n"
"    ...     (cre(0), cre(1), ann(1), ann(0)): 0.25  # four-body term (order 4)\n"
"    ... })\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Filter to keep only terms of order 2\n"
"    >>> order_two_terms = [\n"
"    ...     (term, coeff) for term, coeff in op.iter_terms()\n"
"    ...     if len(term) == 2\n"
"    ... ]\n"
"    >>>\n"
"    >>> # Reconstruct operator from filtered terms\n"
"    >>> filtered_op = FermionOperator.from_terms(order_two_terms)\n"
"    >>> print(f\"Original operator has {len(op)} terms\")\n"
"    Original operator has 3 terms\n"
"    >>> print(f\"Filtered operator has {len(filtered_op)} term\")\n"
"    Filtered operator has 1 term\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    ```c\n"
"    // WARNING: Term iteration and filtering are not yet available in the C API.\n"
"    ```\n"
"  </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""

