# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The [`OperatorTrait.normal_ordered()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.normal_ordered \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.normal_ordered\") protocol method leaves its positional and keyword arguments deliberately unspecified, allowing concrete operator implementations to define adjustable parameters that control the exact canonical form produced. This enables operator-specific optimizations and normal form variants tailored to their algebra or use case. Check the API documentation for your operator type to see what parameters are available.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hint\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Sadyang hindi tinutukoy ng protocol method na [`OperatorTrait.normal_ordered()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.normal_ordered \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.normal_ordered\") ang mga positional at keyword argument nito, kaya puwedeng magtakda ang mga konkretong implementasyon ng operator ng mga adjustable na parameter na kumokontrol sa eksaktong canonical form na nagagawa. Nagbibigay-daan ito sa mga optimization na partikular sa operator at mga variant ng normal form na akma sa kanilang algebra o gamit. Tingnan ang API documentation ng uri ng operator mo para makita ang mga available na parameter.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
